ASV (ARM64 assembly viewer)
===========================

This repository contains the ASV Android application source (Kotlin, resources,
Gradle) and a prebuilt native library used at runtime.

Application source
------------------
The Kotlin/UI/Gradle files in this repository are the ASV application. They do
not include the analysis engine's C/C++ source, headers, CMake, or static
libraries. Copyright in the application source remains with the ASV authors.
This file does not grant a license to the engine.

Prebuilt native library (not open source)
-----------------------------------------
app/src/main/jniLibs/arm64-v8a/libicode_jni.so is a precompiled shared library
that provides the analysis and replay implementation through a JNI interface
(load name: icode_jni). It is distributed only as a binary. This repository
does not publish engine source, and it does not grant an open-source license
for that library or for the engine inside it. Do not treat libicode_jni.so as
being licensed under an MIT, Apache, GPL, or other open-source grant from this
project.

The ELF debug symbol table of the shipped .so was stripped. That does not make
the binary irreversible or free of all build metadata. In particular, some
third-party code statically compiled into the library (notably Z3) still
contains source-path string literals from the machine that built those
dependencies. Those strings are not complete debug symbols, but they are not
fully removed.

libc++_shared.so
----------------
app/src/main/jniLibs/arm64-v8a/libc++_shared.so is the LLVM libc++ shared
runtime used by the Android NDK. It is subject to the LLVM license and the
NCSA/MIT-style terms that accompany libc++ (see the LLVM project and the
Android NDK notices).

Third-party code that may be statically present inside libicode_jni.so
---------------------------------------------------------------------
The prebuilt engine library is believed to statically incorporate, among other
components, publicly known projects such as:

  - Capstone disassembly engine (BSD license; upstream: capstone-engine)
  - Triton binary analysis framework (Apache-2.0; upstream: Jonathan Salwan /
    quarkslab)
  - Z3 theorem prover (MIT license; upstream: Microsoft Research)
  - Keystone assembler (GPL-2.0; upstream: keystone-engine)

Presence of these projects in the binary was inferred from exported or
internal symbols and strings, not from publishing their sources here.
Redistribution of those components remains subject to their original licenses.
This notice is informational. It does not relicense those projects, and it
does not claim that the ASV authors can offer Keystone (GPL-2.0) or any other
component under a different license. Recipients who need to verify license
compliance for a public distribution should review the corresponding upstream
terms themselves.

No rights in the proprietary engine are waived.
